def LAD(*a): return list(a)
def RUB(a,b,c,d): return [(a,'Missing or unclear','Meets the stated check',b),(c,'Guessing','Evidence kept',d),('Records','Gaps','Complete','Complete and reviewed by a peer'),('Safety and ethics','Overlooked','Followed','Followed and taught to others')]
COURSES = [
dict(slug='social-media-management', title='Social Media Management', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Plan, publish and measure content for a small organisation across social channels, with care for people, consent and privacy.',
 outs=[('Define','a goal with a number and an audience for each channel.'),('Apply','a content calendar, post formats and a reply routine.'),('Analyse','reach, engagement and conversion from real numbers.'),('Evaluate','risks such as false claims, copyright and unhappy comments.'),('Create','a 30-day plan and a results report.')],
 task='Run a 30-day content plan for a small organisation and report the results with real numbers.', cond='About 8 weeks part-time. A practice or real organisation account, free design and scheduling tools, a phone, a mentor.',
 standard='Every post is accurate, credited and scheduled; replies are polite and answered within 24 hours; the report compares results with the goal using real numbers.', who='Marketers, small business owners, students, community volunteers.', req='Comfort using a smartphone and social apps.',
 mods=[
 M('Set goals and know the audience','Define',4,['Write one goal with a number and a date, such as 200 new local followers in 30 days.','Describe the audience by age range, city, language and the hours they are online.','Choose two channels where that audience already spends time.','List what success looks like beyond followers: enquiries, visits, orders.'],'A bakery wants 40 cake enquiries a month. Its buyers are women aged 25 to 40 in one city who use Hindi and English, so it picks a photo channel and a messaging channel.','Write a goal, an audience profile and a two-channel choice for one organisation.','The goal has a number and date, and the audience profile has at least four facts.','Why choose only two channels at first?','A small team can post well on two; spreading thin lowers quality and results.'),
 M('Plan content pillars and voice','Create',4,['Choose three pillars: teach, show, ask.','Mix formats: photo, short video, carousel, text.','Write a voice guide of five do and don\'t rules, including language mix.','Check each pillar against the goal.'],'Pillars for the bakery: baking tips (teach), order-day behind the scenes (show), flavour polls (ask); voice is warm, short, Hinglish allowed, no slang for customers over 50.','Create a pillar plan and a voice guide for your organisation.','Each pillar links to the goal and the guide has five rules.','What is a content pillar?','A repeating theme that every post belongs to.'),
 M('Build a calendar and schedule','Apply',5,['Set a weekly rhythm, such as three posts and two stories per week.','Batch create: make one week of posts in one sitting.','Mark festivals, exam seasons and local events on the calendar.','Use a free scheduling tool and keep a backup copy of every file.'],'Three posts a week for 30 days is 13 posts. Batching 4 posts takes 2 hours instead of 4 separate 1-hour sessions.','Fill a 30-day calendar with dates, pillars, formats and times.','All 30 days are planned and each post has an owner and a posting time.','Why batch the creation of posts?','It saves set-up time and keeps the calendar full.'),
 M('Write and design posts','Apply',6,['Open with a hook in the first line, give one useful point, end with one clear action.','Write captions in the language the audience uses; add alt text for images.','Use only images and music you own or have rights to, and credit sources.','Get written or recorded consent before showing any person, especially a child.'],'Hook: "Why does your cake sink in the middle?" Value: oven temperature 10 degrees too low. Action: "Message us the word TIPS for a free checklist."','Create ten posts with captions, images and a credit or consent note for each.','All ten posts have a hook, a single action, and consent or credit recorded.','What belongs in every caption?','A hook, a useful point and one clear action.'),
 M('Short video and visual basics','Create',5,['Shoot vertical video in daylight with the phone held steady or on a stand.','Keep clips under 30 seconds and put the key message in the first 3 seconds.','Add captions because many viewers watch without sound.','Keep text inside the safe area so buttons do not cover it.'],'A 20-second video with 5 clips of 4 seconds each, captions on, and the offer shown in the first 3 seconds.','Shoot and edit three short videos with captions.','Each video is under 30 seconds, captioned and readable on a small screen.','Why add captions to video?','Many people watch with the sound off.'),
 M('Community, replies and crises','Evaluate',5,['Answer comments and messages within 24 hours using a short reply guide.','Never share personal details such as phone numbers or addresses in public replies.','Handle a complaint in three steps: thank, move to private, solve and report back.','Hide abuse, report threats, and log every serious case.'],'A customer posts that a cake arrived late. Reply in 2 hours, ask for the order number by private message, offer a refund or redo, and log the case.','Write a reply guide with five sample replies and a crisis checklist.','Replies are polite, safe and fit the checklist.','Why move a complaint to a private message?','It protects personal details and lets you solve it without a public argument.'),
 M('Measure and improve','Analyse',5,['Record reach, engagement rate, link clicks and enquiries every week.','Work out engagement rate: interactions divided by reach, times 100.','Find the best and worst three posts and ask why.','Change one thing for the next week and test it.'],'A post reached 2,000 people with 120 likes, comments and shares: 6% engagement. A text post reached 1,500 with 15: 1%. Make more of the first kind.','Fill a weekly results sheet for four weeks and write three findings.','Numbers are correct and each finding leads to one action.','How is engagement rate worked out?','Interactions divided by reach, times 100.'),
 M('Capstone: 30-day plan and report','Create',6,['Run the full 30-day plan with scheduling and replies.','Compare results with the goal using real numbers.','Report what worked, what failed and what you will change.','Present the report to the organisation and agree the next month.'],'Goal 200 followers: result 164 followers, 31 enquiries, best content was a how-to video at 7% engagement. Next month: two videos a week.','Present a 30-day report with the calendar, results and next plan.','The report shows goal against result, evidence from at least three posts, and next steps with dates.','What makes a social report useful?','It compares real results with the goal and leads to clear next steps.')],
 extra=[('When should you ask permission to post a photo?','Before posting, always for people and always in writing for children.'),('What should you do if you find a post with a wrong fact?','Correct it quickly, say what changed, and log it.')],
 rubric=RUB('Plan','Goal, calendar and results all linked with numbers','Content quality','Accurate, credited, consented and consistent in voice'),
 ladder=LAD('Use social media safely and kindly.','Post with a hook and a clear action.','Plan and schedule a month for one channel.','Run several channels and report with numbers.','Lead a content team and set the monthly strategy.','Direct social strategy and risk policy for an organisation.','Set professional standards for social media practice.'),
 jobs=['Social media executive','Content creator','Community manager','Digital marketing assistant','Freelance social media manager']),

dict(slug='sme-msme-development', title='SME and MSME Development', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Start, formalise and grow a small enterprise: choosing a legal form, registration, records, cash flow, markets, compliance and government support schemes.',
 outs=[('Define','the enterprise type, size class and legal form.'),('Apply','registration, licences and daily records.'),('Analyse','cost, margin, break-even and cash flow.'),('Evaluate','funding options and support schemes.'),('Create','a growth plan with dated actions.')],
 task='Prepare a registration-ready, finance-ready growth plan for a real or practice small enterprise.', cond='About 10 weeks part-time. A real or practice enterprise, access to government portals, a spreadsheet, a mentor.',
 standard='Documents are complete, cash flow is forecast for 12 months with every figure traced to a source, compliance dates are on a calendar, and the plan has dated actions.', who='Founders, artisans, shop owners, farm-based producers, development workers.', req='Basic arithmetic. An enterprise idea or a running small business.',
 mods=[
 M('Enterprise types and size classes','Define',4,['Know the size classes: micro, small and medium, set by investment and turnover limits in current rules.','Compare sole proprietor, partnership, limited liability partnership and company.','Match the form to liability, tax, number of owners and funding needs.','Check the latest limits on the official portal before deciding.'],'A tailoring unit with one owner, 6 workers and yearly sales of 18 lakh fits a sole proprietorship in the micro class. Two partners adding machines may prefer a partnership.','Choose a legal form and a size class for your enterprise and justify them.','Choice cites the current limits and names one risk of the form chosen.','Why does the legal form matter?','It sets liability, tax, ownership and how you can raise funds.'),
 M('Registration and licences','Apply',6,['Register on the government portal for small enterprises with an identity number and business activity codes.','Check if GST registration is needed by turnover and type of sale.','List local licences: shop and establishment, food safety, trade or pollution consent as relevant.','Keep scanned and printed copies and a renewal date for each.'],'A food unit needs registration as a micro enterprise, food safety licence, local trade licence and GST once turnover passes the state threshold. Each gets a renewal date.','Build a registration and licence checklist for your enterprise.','Every document is listed with the issuing office, documents needed and renewal date.','Why keep renewal dates?','Lapsed licences can stop trade and attract penalties.'),
 M('Records and bookkeeping','Apply',6,['Record every sale and expense on the day in a cash book.','Separate personal money from business money in a bank account.','Keep bills, invoices and receipts in dated folders.','Close the books monthly and compare with the bank statement.'],'Opening cash Rs 20,000; sales Rs 90,000; expenses Rs 62,000; closing cash should be Rs 48,000. If the bank shows Rs 45,000, find the Rs 3,000 gap.','Keep a cash book for 30 days and reconcile it to bank.','Closing balance matches the bank, or each difference is explained.','Why separate personal and business money?','Without it, profit and loss cannot be known.'),
 M('Costing, pricing and break-even','Analyse',6,['Split costs into fixed (rent, salary) and variable (material, packing).','Work out cost per unit and margin.','Break-even units equal fixed costs divided by selling price minus variable cost.','Test price changes of 5 to 10 percent against sales volume.'],'Fixed cost Rs 30,000 a month; price Rs 150 a unit; variable cost Rs 90 a unit. Margin Rs 60 a unit. Break-even is 500 units a month.','Calculate cost per unit, margin and break-even for one product.','Calculations are correct and each input comes from a bill or quote.','How is break-even found?','Fixed costs divided by selling price minus variable cost.'),
 M('Cash flow and working capital','Analyse',6,['List expected cash in and cash out for each of 12 months.','Include delays: customers pay in 30 to 60 days, suppliers want advance.','Find the lowest closing balance and the month it occurs.','Plan to cover the gap: faster collection, smaller stock or a working capital loan.'],'Month 4 shows cash in 1.2 lakh and out 1.6 lakh, with opening 0.3 lakh: closing minus 0.1 lakh. A gap of Rs 0.1 lakh (Rs 10,000) must be funded.','Build a 12-month cash flow forecast with the funding gap highlighted.','Every month balances and the lowest balance is identified with a plan.','Why can a profitable business run out of cash?','Customers pay late while costs must be paid now.'),
 M('Funding and support schemes','Evaluate',6,['Compare own savings, bank loans, government-backed loan schemes and investor money.','Check eligibility, collateral rules and credit guarantee support on official sites.','Work out the monthly instalment and total interest.','Ask what a lender needs: registration, bank statements, project report.'],'A loan of 5 lakh at 12% for 3 years has an instalment near Rs 16,600 a month, total repaid near Rs 5.98 lakh. The unit must earn that surplus.','Compare two funding options for your plan and choose one.','Comparison shows the monthly instalment and whether cash flow can bear it.','What must you check before taking a loan?','Whether monthly cash surplus can pay the instalment.'),
 M('Markets, customers and compliance calendar','Apply',5,['Find three customer groups and the channels to reach them: local retail, wholesale, online marketplace, government purchase.','Register on a government procurement portal if selling to public buyers.','File returns and pay dues on time: GST, income tax, provident fund and state insurance if applicable.','Put every due date on a shared calendar with a named owner.'],'A craft unit sells 60% locally, 25% via an online marketplace and 15% to a wholesale buyer. Suppose a GST return is due on the 20th (check the current due date with the tax authority); the owner then books the 15th for preparation.','Produce a market list and a 12-month compliance calendar.','Calendar covers every filing with a date and owner, and the market list names three groups.','Why use a compliance calendar?','It prevents missed dates and penalties.'),
 M('Capstone: growth plan','Create',6,['Combine registration, records, costing, cash flow, funding and markets into one plan.','Set three growth goals with numbers and dates.','List risks and a response for each.','Present to a mentor or lender and record feedback.'],'Plan to raise sales from 6 lakh to 9 lakh in 12 months by adding a second market, with a 2 lakh working capital need and a risk plan for late payments.','Present the growth plan with all supporting sheets.','Plan is consistent across sheets, goals are dated and risks have responses.','What makes a growth plan credible?','Numbers from real records, consistent sheets and dated actions.')],
 extra=[('What is working capital?','Money needed to run daily operations between paying costs and receiving sales.'),('Why check scheme rules on the official site?','Limits and conditions change, and old information can be wrong.')],
 rubric=RUB('Finance','Forecast traced to records and tested for gaps','Compliance','All dates calendared with owners and reviewed monthly'),
 ladder=LAD('Know what an enterprise is.','Keep simple daily records.','Register and file for a micro enterprise.','Cost, price and forecast cash flow.','Prepare funding applications and lead growth.','Advise many enterprises or run a support programme.','Shape enterprise policy and support across a region.'),
 jobs=['Enterprise development officer','Business advisory associate','Loan and scheme facilitator','Small business accountant','Self-employed entrepreneur']),

dict(slug='consulting', title='Consulting and Advisory Practice', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Work as an adviser: scope problems, gather evidence, compare options, recommend and present, and follow up on results.',
 outs=[('Define','a client problem in a sentence with an outcome and limits.'),('Apply','issue trees, hypotheses and interview plans.'),('Analyse','data and interviews to find root causes.'),('Evaluate','options against agreed criteria.'),('Create','a recommendation deck and a dated action plan.')],
 task='Complete a small advisory project with a written recommendation and a client presentation.', cond='About 8 weeks part-time. A real or mock client, sample data in a spreadsheet, a mentor.',
 standard='The problem is scoped, evidence is shown with sources, options are scored against criteria, and next steps have owners and dates.', who='Analysts, professionals, freelancers, managers moving into advisory roles.', req='Basic spreadsheet skills and clear writing.',
 mods=[
 M('Scope the problem','Define',5,['Ask who, what, why now and what will be done with the answer.','Agree the outcome, the limits, the time and the data available.','Write a one-page scope with a measurable target.','Confirm in writing before starting.'],'Scope: reduce late deliveries from 20% to 10% in 3 months across one city, using order data for the last 6 months; no change to vehicle count.','Write a one-page scope for a client problem.','Scope has outcome, numbers, limits, deadline and data source.','What belongs in a scope?','Outcome, limits, time and available data.'),
 M('Structure the problem','Apply',5,['Build an issue tree so branches do not overlap and cover the whole problem.','Write hypotheses you can prove or disprove with data.','List the analysis each hypothesis needs.','Prioritise the branches that could explain most of the gap.'],'Late deliveries split into dispatch delay, route delay and handover delay. Hypothesis: dispatch delay causes over half of lateness.','Build an issue tree and five hypotheses for your scope.','Branches do not overlap and each hypothesis can be tested.','What does an issue tree do?','Breaks a problem into separate parts that together cover it.'),
 M('Plan and run interviews','Apply',5,['Choose interviewees from different levels and functions.','Write open questions and avoid leading ones.','Record notes, quotes and follow-ups, with consent.','Mark each claim as fact, opinion or rumour.'],'Ask a dispatcher "Walk me through yesterday morning" instead of "Don\'t you think the route planning is bad?". Six interviews yield 14 claims; 8 are confirmed by data.','Run three interviews and write a notes sheet.','Questions are open and every note is tagged fact, opinion or rumour.','Why avoid leading questions?','They push the answer and hide the real view.'),
 M('Collect and clean data','Apply',6,['List the data needed and who owns it.','Check for missing values, duplicates and wrong units.','Keep an untouched copy of the raw file.','Record each cleaning step so another person can repeat it.'],'A file of 4,200 orders has 120 duplicates and 85 blank delivery times. After cleaning, 3,995 rows remain and the log lists each step.','Clean a sample dataset and keep a change log.','Raw copy is kept, log is complete and row counts reconcile.','Why keep the raw file untouched?','So any step can be checked or repeated.'),
 M('Analyse and find root causes','Analyse',6,['Use pivot tables to cut data by branch, time and type.','Look for the few causes behind most of the gap.','Test each hypothesis and say what evidence confirms or rejects it.','Ask why five times to move from symptom to root.'],'Of 800 late orders, 480 (60%) left the warehouse after 11:00. Root cause: packing starts only after morning stock is counted.','Test your hypotheses with data and write a findings page.','Each finding has a number, a chart and the data source.','What is a root cause?','The underlying reason which, if fixed, stops the problem.'),
 M('Generate and compare options','Evaluate',6,['List at least three options including "do nothing".','Agree criteria with the client: impact, cost, time, risk.','Score each option from 1 to 5 and weigh the criteria.','Check the sums and show the working.'],'Option A, start packing at 7:00: impact 5, cost 4, time 4, risk 4. Option B, hire two riders: impact 3, cost 2, time 3, risk 3. Weights 40/20/20/20 make A 4.4 and B 2.8.','Score three options against four criteria with weights.','Criteria are agreed, scores are justified and totals are correct.','Why include "do nothing" as an option?','It shows the cost of not acting.'),
 M('Write the recommendation','Create',5,['Lead with the answer, then give three supporting reasons.','Use one message per slide and a headline that states the point.','Show the numbers, the risks and the cost.','End with next steps that have owners and dates.'],'Headline: "Start packing at 7:00 to cut late deliveries from 20% to 11% by month 3". Three reasons: root cause, cost, speed.','Write a ten-slide recommendation deck.','Every slide has a headline that states the point, and next steps have owners and dates.','Why lead with the answer?','Busy readers get the point first and can read detail if they want.'),
 M('Present, handle questions and follow up','Create',5,['Rehearse the talk to a time limit of 15 minutes.','Answer questions with facts and say "I will check" when unsure.','Agree a date to review results with the client.','Track the target after 30 and 90 days.'],'After 90 days late deliveries are 12%. Report a gap of 2 points to target and propose a second packing shift.','Present to a mentor, record questions and write a follow-up note.','Presentation is on time, questions are logged, and a review date is agreed.','Why follow up after the project?','To confirm results and fix what did not work.')],
 extra=[('How do you keep client information safe?','Share it only with those who need it, store it securely and delete it when the work ends.'),('What should you do when the data contradicts what the client expects?','Show the evidence calmly, explain the limits and let the client decide.')],
 rubric=RUB('Evidence','Every claim backed by data or a source','Recommendation','Clear, costed and with dated next steps'),
 ladder=LAD('Ask good questions and listen.','Break a problem into parts.','Gather and clean data for a small project.','Lead a small advisory project.','Manage several projects and a small team.','Lead an advisory practice and client relationships.','Set standards and method for advisory work across a profession.'),
 jobs=['Business analyst','Associate consultant','Management consultant','Independent adviser','Project analyst']),
]
